We could certainly make one up, but I'm not sure
the game really needs a lot of new artifact weapons.
In particular, chaotically aligned weapon artifacts
are rather limited by design, I think:  the only really
powerful one has major serious drawbacks.  That's
part of the balance between the alignments:  lawful
characters get unambiguously fantastic weapon
artifacts; neutrals get unbelievably spectacular
non-weapon artifacts; and chaotics can get away
with more dastardly behavior and have an easier
time in Gehennom (especially on the way back up).
For a weapon, most chaotics end up using an
unaligned artifact, or a non-artifact weapon, or
maybe a non-intelligent artifact that blasts them.
I'm not sure you want to disrupt that balance.

You got around this with the quest artifact by
making it neutral, which is possible because your
own quest artifact gets its alignment adjusted,
but I don't know if the same trick would work
for sacrifice gifts.  Would it?  Wait, doesn't
Magicbane get adjusted for Wizards?  Hmmm...


